Evidence Collected

The following evidence was collected during the research:

Completed questionnaires from five participants.
Notes from participant responses.
Summary of common challenges and user suggestions.
Main Challenges Identified

The participants highlighted the following problems:

Long waiting times.
Overcrowded service offices.
Uncertainty about queue progress.
Missing classes or other activities while waiting.
Lack of information on estimated waiting time.
Proposed Solution

Based on the research findings, participants recommended a mobile application that would allow users to:

Join a virtual queue remotely.
View their current queue position.
Receive real-time notifications.
Track estimated waiting time.
Confirm service completion after being served.